hi--

I guess one thing to keep in mind is that if you want to interpret the 
results of the random effects estimation (meaning the variance 
components), you will have to impute under that model as well.  Doing so 
is kind of a nuisance (you could use the package pan).  One alternative 
is to impute a wide file (meaning y1,y2, x,z ....), but that's not very 
useful if the problem is very difficult. 

i'd be curious how you imputed under a random-effects specification?

regards,
michael

